        <StdOut>Set apart for Firefox: F-5: Firefox shades a pattern whose tile is a pixel or two across a few levels lighter than Chromium, from the one tile the document gives; each lies within F-1's tolerance of the reference. Firefox's image of teanwest has 32165 pixels outside the tolerance of Chromium's (each color channel within the range the other image takes within 1 pixel, give or take 4 levels, or at an edge within 80 levels of it, and within 0.4 of the contrast around it, once both are blurred by 1 pixel), by up to 9 levels; see browsers/firefox/differences/teanwest.png.</StdOut>
